   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "test7_fmc_step20_cell_18_64",
     "description": "Reference: NCAR fire_behavior test7 (80 x 80 fire mesh, dx = dy = 25 m, dt = 0.5 s) with the fuel-moisture model on, step 20 (ts = 10 s), fire cell (18, 64), Anderson category 2. Every expected value is a real32 Fortran dump of the run data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_fmc: the fuel table and Rothermel parameters from esm_dump_ros_params_20.json, the moisture classes from esm_dump_fmc_20.json and esm_dump_fmc_avg_20.json, the rate of spread and level-set tendency from Runge-Kutta stage 1 (esm_dump_ls_tend_58.json), the ignition time from esm_dump_ls_tign_20.json, the fuel fraction from esm_dump_fuel_left_20.json, the flame length from esm_dump_flame_20.json and the heat fluxes from esm_dump_fire_flux_20.json. rel 1e-5 throughout except where the description of an assertion says otherwise. The document has 6400 level-set ODE states and every assertion is at t = 0, so the time span is empty (esm-spec 6.6.2) and the runner answers from the initial state without integrating. THE MID-FLAME WIND IS NOW COUPLED, not prescribed (2026-09-21): uf and vf at the fire cell are produced by FireWindWRFFire interpolating the atmosphere profile of column (5,16) logarithmically to 1 m and FireWindHinterpWRFFire interpolating the resulting 19 x 19 atmosphere field bilinearly onto fire cell (18,64). Only the atmosphere profile of that one column, and the fractional atmosphere-grid coordinates of the fire mesh, are still prescribed -- both are genuinely external to the fire model.",
     "parameter_overrides": {},
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 0
     },
     "tolerance": {
      "rel": 1e-05
     },
